# ── Privacy boundary (RISKS P-01, ADR-0007) ─────────────────────────────
# Real career data NEVER enters this public repo. The committed
# docs/profile.example/ (fictional) is used by tests, fixtures, and demos.
docs/profile/

# Secrets — .env.example (documented variable names only) is committed
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local data: database dumps, backups, exports of real postings/applications.
# Dumps of dev contain real profile rows — no dump naming variant may ever be
# commit-eligible. /*.sql only ignores repo-root files (a plain-format pg_dump
# landing there); committed migrations live under packages/db/migrations/.
*.dump
*.backup
*.sql.gz
/*.sql
backups/
exports/
# M13-01: the profile tar + row-count manifest db:backup mints (belt-and-suspenders;
# these live OUTSIDE the repo by enforced check, but never let one become commit-eligible).
# The .age variants are the NC-1(b) cloud branch's encrypted dump + tar.
careerforge-profile-*.tar
careerforge-profile-*.tar.age
careerforge-db-*.manifest.json
careerforge-db-*.dump.age

# ── Dependencies & build output ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
# pnpm store, should it ever land in-repo (the devcontainer pins its store
# to a container path; this is belt-and-suspenders for a public repo).
.pnpm-store/
dist/
# `nuxt generate` drops a convenience symlink `dist -> .output/public` at the
# app root; the `dist/` rule above matches directories only, so name the link.
apps/*/dist
.output/
.nuxt/
.nitro/
# Nuxt Content's build-time SQLite database (regenerated every build).
.data/
coverage/
# Lighthouse CI reports (LHR json/html), regenerated by `pnpm lighthouse` (M2-03).
.lighthouseci/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── OS / editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
# settings.json is deliberately committed: mechanism B (RISKS S-03) hides
# .env from the editor surface and must survive fresh clones.
!.vscode/settings.json

# ── Playwright run artifacts (e2e traces may embed rendered pages) ──────
test-results/
playwright-report/

# ---- Terraform (M10-06): local state + operator tfvars never committed ----
# example.tfvars (fictional, name-only) IS committed; terraform.tfvars (real
# operator values) and ALL state are ignored. State carries no secret (ADR-0022
# D4), so this is a durability concern only. .terraform.lock.hcl is committed
# (reproducible provider pins) and deliberately NOT ignored here.
infra/terraform/.terraform/
infra/terraform/*.tfstate
infra/terraform/*.tfstate.*
infra/terraform/*.tfvars
!infra/terraform/example.tfvars
# Saved plan files (terraform plan -out=...) can embed variable values (M10-08
# finding: a stray `tfplan` was left untracked-but-not-ignored after the go-live
# ceremony). Never commit them.
infra/terraform/tfplan
infra/terraform/*.tfplan

# @nuxt/test-utils writes a version stamp into each app's .nuxtrc on every
# toolchain run; tracking them makes clean trees dirty themselves after any
# test-utils bump (PR#188 drift, notes/nuxtrc-stamp-drift-2026-08-13.md).
# Tool-owned, stamp-only files - untracked by decision.
.nuxtrc
